herramientas de línea de comandos","Estructura de directorios personalizable"],"fr":["Architecture de référence pour provisionner des environnements de développement","Prise en charge de Homebrew, apt et winget","Configuration via le fichier jarvy.toml","Intégration avec des outils en ligne de commande","Structure de répertoires personnalisable"],"de":["Referenzarchitektur für die Bereitstellung von Entwicklungsumgebungen","Unterstützung für Homebrew, apt und winget","Konfiguration über die Datei jarvy.toml","Integration mit Kommandozeilen-Tools","Anpassbare Verzeichnisstruktur"],"pt":["Provisionamento de ambientes de desenvolvimento com Jarvy CLI","Gerenciamento de pacotes nativos com Homebrew, apt/dnf e winget","Estrutura de diretório personalizada para projetos Jarvy","Integração com testes de integração","Suporte a configuração via arquivo jarvy.toml"],"ru":["Обеспечение среды разработки с помощью Jarvy CLI для ИИ Агентов","Управление родными пакетами с помощью Homebrew, apt/dnf и winget","Пользовательская структура директории для проектов Jarvy","Интеграция с интеграционными тестами","Поддержка конфигурации через файл jarvy.toml"],"ar":["توفير بيئات التطوير باستخدام Jarvy CLI لـ AI Tools","إدارة الحزم الأصلية باستخدام Homebrew و apt/dnf و winget","هيكل دليل مخصص لمشاريع Jarvy","التكامل مع اختبارات التكامل","دعم التكوين عبر ملف jarvy.toml"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use agentic-jumpstart-architecture","what is agentic-jumpstart-architecture","agentic-jumpstart-architecture alternative","agentic-jumpstart-architecture vs Jarvy","agentic-jumpstart-architecture install","agentic-jumpstart-architecture setup guide","Jarvy CLI project setup","native package manager integration","jarvy.toml config file"],"zh":["AI开发工具","Jarvy CLI","agentic-jumpstart-architecture","跨平台开发环境","native package managers","配置文件","CLI入口点"],"ja":["AI開発ツール","Jarvy CLI","agentic-jumpstart-architecture","クロスプラットフォーム開発環境","ネイティブパッケージマネージャー","設定ファイル","CLIエントリーポイント"],"ko":["AI 개발 도구","Jarvy CLI","agentic-jumpstart-architecture","크로스 플랫폼 개발 환경","네이티브 패키지 매니저","설정 파일","CLI 엔트리 포인트"],"es":["Agentic Jumpstart","arquitectura de desarrollo","herramientas de línea de comandos","provisionamiento de entornos","Homebrew","apt","winget","jarvy.toml","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Agentic Jumpstart","architecture de développement","outils en ligne de commande","provisionnement d''environnements","Homebrew","apt","winget","jarvy.toml","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Agentic Jumpstart","Entwicklungsarchitektur","Kommandozeilen-Tools","Bereitstellung von Umgebungen","Homebrew","apt","winget","jarvy.toml","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Agentic-Jumpstart","Jarvy CLI","provisionamento de ambientes","gerenciamento de pacotes","desenvolvimento de software","arquitetura de projeto","Jarvy TOML","Homebrew","apt/dnf","winget"],"ru":["Agentic-Jumpstart","Jarvy CLI","обеспечение среды разработки","управление пакетами","разработка программного обеспечения","архитектура проекта","Jarvy TOML","Homebrew","apt/dnf","winget","ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["Agentic-Jumpstart","Jarvy CLI","توفير بيئات التطوير","إدارة الحزم","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة المشروع","Jarvy TOML","Homebrew","apt/dnf","winget","AI Tools"]}},"owner":"bearbinary","repo":"Jarvy","repoPath":"bearbinary/Jarvy","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.580Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agentic-jumpstart-architecture","description":"Architecture guidelines for Jarvy CLI - codebase structure, tool implementation patterns, registry system, platform-specific code organization, and module conventions.","bodyPreview":"# Jarvy Architecture Guidelines\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive architecture guidance for the Jarvy CLI project.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nJarvy is a cross-platform CLI tool that provisions development environments from a `jarvy.toml` config file using native package managers (Homebrew, apt/dnf, winget).\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\njarvy/\n├── src/\n│   ├── main.rs              # CLI entry point (clap derive macros)\n│   ├── lib.rs               # Public re-exports for integration tests\n│   ├── con","body":"# Jarvy Architecture Guidelines\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive architecture guidance for the Jarvy CLI project.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nJarvy is a cross-platform CLI tool that provisions development environments from a `jarvy.toml` config file using native package managers (Homebrew, apt/dnf, winget).\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\njarvy/\n├── src/\n│   ├── main.rs              # CLI entry point (clap derive macros)\n│   ├── lib.rs               # Public re-exports for integration tests\n│   ├── config.rs            # jarvy.toml parsing with serde\n│   ├── error_codes.rs       # Standardized exit codes\n│   ├── analytics.rs         # OpenTelemetry/tracing setup\n│   ├── posthog.rs           # PostHog analytics client\n│   ├── setup.rs             # Setup command implementation\n│   ├── bootstrap.rs         # Bootstrap command implementation\n│   ├── init.rs              # Global initialization logic\n│   ├── report.rs            # Tool status reporting\n│   ├── provisioner.rs       # Core provisioning orchestration\n│   ├── tools/\n│   │   ├── mod.rs           # Tool module registry and re-exports\n│   │   ├── registry.rs      # Global OnceLock<RwLock<HashMap>> registry\n│   │   ├── common.rs        # Shared utilities\n│   │   ├── _template.rs     # Scaffold template for new tools\n│   │   └── {tool}/          # Tool implementations\n│   │       ├── mod.rs       # Re-exports the handler\n│   │       └── {tool}.rs    # Implementation\n│   └── tests/               # Unit test modules\n├── tests/                   # Integration tests\n├── crates/\n│   └── cargo-jarvy/         # Cargo subcommand for scaffolding\n└── Cargo.toml\n```\n\n## Core Patterns\n\n### 1. Tool Implementation Pattern\n\nEvery tool follows a three-layer architecture:\n\n```rust\n// src/tools/{name}/{name}.rs\n\nuse crate::tools::common::{InstallError, cmd_satisfies, has, run};\n#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\nuse crate::tools::common::{detect_linux_pm, PkgOps, default_use_sudo};\n\n/// Registry adapter: allows tools::add(\"{name}\", version) to dispatch here\npub fn add_handler(min_hint: &str) -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    ensure(min_hint)\n}\n\n/// Main entry: probe first; install if needed\npub fn ensure(min_hint: &str) -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    if cmd_satisfies(\"{binary}\", min_hint) {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n    install()\n}\n\nfn install() -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]\n    { return install_macos(); }\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\n    { return install_linux(); }\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"windows\")]\n    { return install_windows(); }\n    #[allow(unreachable_code)]\n    Err(InstallError::Unsupported)\n}\n\n#[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]\nfn install_macos() -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    if !has(\"brew\") {\n        return Err(InstallError::Prereq(\"Homebrew not found. Install https://brew.sh\"));\n    }\n    run(\"brew\", &[\"install\", \"{formula}\"])?;\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\nfn install_linux() -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    let pm = detect_linux_pm().ok_or(InstallError::Prereq(\n        \"No supported package manager (apt/dnf/yum/zypper/pacman/apk)\"\n    ))?;\n    let _ = PkgOps::update(pm, default_use_sudo());\n    PkgOps::install(pm, \"{package}\", default_use_sudo())\n}\n\n#[cfg(target_os = \"windows\")]\nfn install_windows() -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    if !has(\"winget\") {\n        return Err(InstallError::Prereq(\"winget not found\"));\n    }\n    run(\"winget\", &[\"install\", \"-e\", \"--id\", \"{WingetId}\"])?;\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Registry Pattern\n\nTools are registered in a global thread-safe registry:\n\n```rust\n// src/tools/registry.rs\nuse std::sync::{OnceLock, RwLock};\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\npub type ToolAdder = fn(version: &str) -> Result<(), InstallError>;\n\nstatic REGISTRY: OnceLock<RwLock<HashMap<String, ToolAdder>>> = OnceLock::new();\n\nfn registry() -> &''static RwLock<HashMap<String, ToolAdder>> {\n    REGISTRY.get_or_init(|| RwLock::new(HashMap::new()))\n}\n\npub fn register_tool(name: &str, handler: ToolAdder) -> bool {\n    let key = name.to_ascii_lowercase();\n    let mut map = registry().write().expect(\"registry rwlock poisoned\");\n    map.insert(key, handler).is_none()\n}\n\npub fn get_tool(name: &str) -> Option<ToolAdder> {\n    let key = name.to_ascii_lowercase();\n    let map = registry().read().expect(\"registry rwlock poisoned\");\n    map.get(&key).copied()\n}\n\npub fn add(name: &str, version: &str) -> Result<(), InstallError> {\n    let key = name.to_ascii_lowercase();\n    let map = registry().read().expect(\"registry rwlock poisoned\");\n    if let Some(handler) = map.get(&key) {\n        let f = *handler;\n        drop(map);\n        f(version)\n    } else {\n        Err(InstallError::Parse(\"unknown tool\"))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Error Handling Pattern\n\nUse `thiserror` for structured errors:\n\n```rust\n// src/tools/common.rs\n#[derive(thiserror::Error, Debug)]\npub enum InstallError {\n    #[error(\"unsupported platform\")]\n    Unsupported,\n    #[error(\"prerequisite missing: {0}\")]\n    Prereq(&''static str),\n    #[error(\"invalid permissions: {0}\")]\n    InvalidPermissions(&''static str),\n    #[error(\"command failed: {cmd} (code: {code:?})\\n{stderr}\")]\n    CommandFailed { cmd: String, code: Option<i32>, stderr: String },\n    #[error(\"io error: {0}\")]\n    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),\n    #[error(\"parse error: {0}\")]\n    Parse(&''static str),\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Platform Detection Pattern\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Deserialize, serde::Serialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\npub enum Os {\n    Linux,\n    Macos,\n    Windows,\n}\n\npub fn current_os() -> Os {\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]   { Os::Linux }\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]   { Os::Macos }\n    #[cfg(target_os = \"windows\")] { Os::Windows }\n}\n\n#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\npub fn detect_linux_pm() -> Option<PackageManager> {\n    // Returns Apt, Dnf, Yum, Zypper, Pacman, or Apk\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Configuration Pattern\n\nSupport both simple and detailed formats in `jarvy.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[privileges]\nuse_sudo = true\n\n[privileges.per_os]\nlinux = true\nmacos = false\n\n[provisioner]\n# Simple format\ngit = \"2.40\"\n\n# Detailed format\ndocker = { version = \"24.0\", version_manager = true, use_sudo = false }\n```\n\nParsed with serde untagged enums:\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Deserialize)]\n#[serde(untagged)]\npub enum ToolConfig {\n    Detailed { version: String, version_manager: Option<bool>, use_sudo: Option<bool> },\n    Simple(String),\n}\n```\n\n## Adding a New Tool\n\n### Step 1: Create the tool directory\n\n```bash\ncargo run -p cargo-jarvy -- new-tool {toolname}\n# Or manually:\nmkdir -p src/tools/{toolname}\n```\n\n### Step 2: Create mod.rs\n\n```rust\n// src/tools/{toolname}/mod.rs\n#![allow(clippy::module_inception)]\npub mod {toolname};\n```\n\n### Step 3: Create the implementation\n\nUse the template in `src/tools/_template.rs` as a starting point.\n\n### Step 4: Register in src/tools/mod.rs\n\n```rust\n// Add module declaration\npub mod {toolname};\n\n// In register_all():\nlet _ = register_tool(\"{toolname}\", crate::tools::{toolname}::{toolname}::add_handler);\n```\n\n## Common Utilities Reference\n\n### Command Execution\n\n```rust\n// Run a command and capture output\nrun(cmd: &str, args: &[&str]) -> Result<Output, InstallError>\n\n// Run with optional sudo (non-Windows)\nrun_maybe_sudo(use_sudo: bool, cmd: &str, args: &[&str]) -> Result<Output, InstallError>\n\n// Check if command exists on PATH\nhas(cmd: &str) -> bool\n\n// Check if command output contains version prefix\ncmd_satisfies(cmd: &str, min_prefix: &str) -> bool\n\n// Require command or return error\nrequire(cmd: &str, remediation: &''static str) -> Result<(), InstallError>\n\n// Require one of multiple commands\nrequire_any<''a>(candidates: &[&''a str], remediation: &''static str) -> Result<&''a str, InstallError>\n```\n\n### Package Manager Operations\n\n```rust\n// Update package lists\nPkgOps::update(pm: PackageManager, use_sudo: Option<bool>) -> Result<(), InstallError>\n\n// Install a package\nPkgOps::install(pm: PackageManager, pkg: &str, use_sudo: Option<bool>) -> Result<(), InstallError>\n```\n\n## Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Constant | Meaning |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| 0 | SUCCESS | Command completed successfully |\n| 2 | CONFIG_ERROR | jarvy.toml missing or malformed |\n| 3 | PREREQ_MISSING | Required package manager not found |\n| 5 | PERMISSION_REQUIRED | Elevated privileges needed |\n\n## CLI Structure\n\nCommands defined with clap derive:\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Parser)]\n#[clap(name = \"jarvy\", version, author, about)]\nstruct Cli {\n    #[clap(subcommand)]\n    command: Option<Commands>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Subcommand)]\nenum Commands {\n    Setup { #[clap(short, long)] file: String },\n    Bootstrap {},\n    Configure {},\n    Get { file: String, output_format: OutputFormat, output: Option<String> },\n    #[clap(external_subcommand)]\n    External(Vec<String>),\n}\n```\n\n## Telemetry Architecture\n\n- **PostHog**: Product analytics for usage events and errors\n- **OpenTelemetry**: Structured logging via OTLP (HTTP/protobuf)\n- **Configuration**: `~/.jarvy/config.toml` with `telemetry = true/false`\n- **Environment**: `JARVY_OTLP_ENDPOINT` for custom collectors\n\n## Key Dependencies\n\n| Crate | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|\n| clap | CLI parsing with derive macros |\n| serde/toml | Configuration parsing |\n| thiserror | Structured error types |\n| tracing | Logging and instrumentation |\n| opentelemetry-otlp | Telemetry export |\n| inquire | Interactive prompts |\n| assert_cmd | Integration testing |\n\n## Conventions\n\n1. **Rust Edition**: 2024\n2. **Commit Messages**: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`)\n3. **Formatting**: Always run `cargo fmt --all`\n4. **Linting**: `cargo clippy --all-features -- -D warnings` must pass\n5. **Dependencies**: Prefer stdlib and existing deps over new crates\n6. **Platform Code**: Use `#[cfg(target_os = \"...\")]` attributes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:11:52.752Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for CLI Agents needing comprehensive architecture guidance for provisioning development environments from config files.","zh":"非常适合需要全面的架构指导来从配置文件中提供开发环境的CLI代理。","ja":"CLIエージェントがconfigファイルから開発環境をプロビジョニングするための包括的なアーキテクチャガイダンスを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"config 파일에서 개발 환경을 프로비저닝하기 위한 포괄적인 아키텍처 가이드가 필요한 CLI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes CLI que necesitan una guía de arquitectura integral para aprovisionar entornos de desarrollo desde archivos de configuración.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents CLI ayant besoin d''un guide d''architecture complet pour provisionner des environnements de développement à partir de fichiers de configuration.","de":"Perfekt für CLI-Agents, die eine umfassende Architektur-Anleitung für die Bereitstellung von Entwicklungsumgebungen aus Konfigurationsdateien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes CLI que necessitam de orientação arquitetônica abrangente para provisionar ambientes de desenvolvimento a partir de arquivos de configuração.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов CLI, которым требуется всестороннее архитектурное руководство для обеспечения разработки среды из файлов конфигурации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة سطر الأوامر الذي يحتاج إلى إرشادات هندسية شاملة لتهيئة بيئات التطوير من ملفات التهيئة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to provision development environments using native package managers like Homebrew, apt/dnf, and winget, while following a structured directory architecture and leveraging config files like jarvy.toml.","zh":"赋予代理使用本地包管理器（如Homebrew、apt/dnf和winget）来提供开发环境的能力，同时遵循结构化的目录架构并利用类似jarvy.toml的配置文件。","ja":"エージェントがHomebrew、apt/dnf、wingetなどのネイティブパッケージマネージャーを使用して開発環境をプロビジョニングし、構造化されたディレクトリアーキテクチャに従い、jarvy.tomlなどのコンフィグファイルを活用できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 Homebrew, apt/dnf, winget 같은 네이티브 패키지 관리자를 사용하여 개발 환경을 프로비저닝할 수 있도록 하며, 구조화된 디렉토리 아키텍처를 따르고 jarvy.toml 같은 구성 파일을 활용할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovisionar entornos de desarrollo utilizando administradores de paquetes nativos como Homebrew, apt/dnf y winget, mientras siguen una arquitectura de directorio estructurada y aprovechan archivos de configuración como jarvy.toml.","fr":"Permet aux agents de provisionner des environnements de développement en utilisant des gestionnaires de paquets natifs comme Homebrew, apt/dnf et winget, tout en suivant une architecture de répertoire structurée et en exploitant des fichiers de configuration comme jarvy.toml.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Entwicklungsumgebungen mithilfe von nativen Paketmanagern wie Homebrew, apt/dnf und winget bereitzustellen, während sie einer strukturierten Verzeichnisarchitektur folgen und Konfigurationsdateien wie jarvy.toml nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a provisionar ambientes de desenvolvimento usando gerenciadores de pacotes nativos como Homebrew, apt/dnf e winget, seguindo uma arquitetura de diretório estruturada e aproveitando arquivos de configuração como jarvy.toml.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечения разработки среды с помощью родных менеджеров пакетов, таких как Homebrew, apt/dnf и winget, при этом соблюдая структурированную архитектуру директорий и используя файлы конфигурации, такие как jarvy.toml.","ar":"يمكن للعميل توفير بيئات التطوير باستخدام مديري حزم أصليين مثل Homebrew و apt/dnf و winget ، مع اتباع هيكل دليل منظم والاستفادة من ملفات التهيئة مثل jarvy.toml."},"useCases":{"en":["Provisioning development environments from jarvy.toml config files","Generating directory structures for Jarvy projects","Integrating native package managers for seamless dependency installation"],"zh":["从jarvy.toml配置文件中提供开发环境","为Jarvy项目生成目录结构","将本地包管理器集成到无缝依赖安装中"],"ja":["jarvy.tomlコンフィグファイルから開発環境をプロビジョニングする","Jarvyプロジェクトのディレクトリ構造を生成する","ネイティブパッケージマネージャーをシームレスな依存関係インストールに統合する"],"ko":["jarvy.toml 구성 파일에서 개발 환경을 프로비저닝하는 것","Jarvy 프로젝트를 위한 디렉토리 구조를 생성하는 것","네이티브 패키지 관리자를 시ーム리스 의존성 설치에 통합하는 것"],"es":["Aprovisionamiento de entornos de desarrollo desde archivos de configuración jarvy.toml","Generación de estructuras de directorio para proyectos Jarvy","Integración de administradores de paquetes nativos para una instalación de dependencias sin problemas"],"fr":["Provisionnement d''environnements de développement à partir de fichiers de configuration jarvy.toml","Génération de structures de répertoire pour les projets Jarvy","Intégration de gestionnaires de paquets natifs pour une installation de dépendances sans problème"],"de":["Bereitstellung von Entwicklungsumgebungen aus Konfigurationsdateien jarvy.toml","Erzeugung von Verzeichnisstrukturen für Jarvy-Projekte","Integration von nativen Paketmanagern für eine reibungslose Installation von Abhängigkeiten"],"pt":["Provisionar ambientes de desenvolvimento a partir de arquivos de configuração jarvy.toml","Gerar estruturas de diretório para projetos Jarvy","Integrar gerenciadores de pacotes nativos para instalação de dependências sem problemas"],"ru":["Обеспечение разработки среды из файлов конфигурации jarvy.toml","Генерация структур директорий для проектов Jarvy","Интеграция родных менеджеров пакетов для бесшовной установки зависимостей"],"ar":["توفير بيئات التطوير من ملفات التهيئة jarvy.toml","إنشاء هياكل دليل لمشاريع Jarvy","دمج مديري الحزم الأصليين لتثبيت التبعيات بشكل متوافق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires jarvy.toml config file","Limited to native package managers supported by Jarvy"],"zh":["需要jarvy.toml配置文件","仅限Jarvy支持的本地包管理器"],"ja":["jarvy.tomlコンフィグファイルが必要","Jarvyがサポートするネイティブパッケージマネージャーに限定される"],"ko":["jarvy.toml 구성 파일이 필요","Jarvy가 지원하는 네이티브 패키지 관리자로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere archivo de configuración jarvy.toml","Limitado a los administradores de paquetes nativos compatibles con Jarvy"],"fr":["Nécessite un fichier de configuration jarvy.toml","Limité aux gestionnaires de paquets natifs pris en charge par Jarvy"],"de":["Benötigt Konfigurationsdatei jarvy.toml","Begrenzt auf von Jarvy unterstützte native Paketmanager"],"pt":["Exige arquivo de configuração jarvy.toml","Limitado a gerenciadores de pacotes nativos suportados pelo Jarvy"],"ru":["Требует файла конфигурации jarvy.toml","Ограничен родными менеджерами пакетов, поддерживаемыми Jarvy"],"ar":["يتطلب ملف تهيئة jarvy.toml","محدود بمديري الحزم الأصليين المدعومين من Jarvy"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"e4b7fcf27771405ad01ad7e23e25573bf1a97c88c4f0b65f7fa9f30e32d549fe","qualityScore":42}');
